  "question": {
    "text": "A particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">m</mtext></math> moving in the <math><mi>x</mi></math> direction with speed <math><mn>2</mn><mi>v</mi></math> is hit by another particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></math> moving in the <math><mi>y</mi></math> direction with speed <math><mi>v</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If the collision is perfectly inelastic, the percentage loss in the energy during the collision is close to:",
